# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COPYRIGHTED MATERIAL -- never commit, never push.
#
# Roland's firmware, wave ROMs, card dumps and manuals belong to Roland. This repository
# only says WHERE a user must put their own dumps (README.md, "ROMs"); it never carries
# them. Upstream emu110 does track roms/ and waves/*.wav -- this fork deliberately does
# not, which is why its history was started fresh instead of forked (ROADMAP.md, §0).
#
# If you really need to add a binary that matches one of these patterns and is NOT
# copyrighted (a test fixture you generated yourself), use `git add -f` and say why in
# the commit message.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Program and wave ROMs, in every naming scheme seen so far
#   MAME:     u-220_roland_1-0-2.ic8, roland-a_r15179892f_mb834000a-20_226-aa.bin
#   d-tech:   roland_u220_pgm_v1-02_(...).bin, roland_t110_u110_u220_waverom0.bin
#   emu110:   U110v203.BIN, SN-U110-08.bin
*.bin
*.BIN
*.rom
*.ROM
*.ic[0-9]*
*.IC[0-9]*
*.eprom
*.hex
*.mot
*.s19

# MAME ROM sets, NVRAM and state
*.zip
*.7z
*.chd
nvram/
cfg/
sta/

# The roms/ folder holds only its README
roms/*
!roms/README.md

# Decoded sample data and recordings of the factory sounds (derived from the ROMs)
*.wav
*.WAV
*.flac
*.aif
*.aiff
*.mp3
*.ogg
*.raw

# SysEx dumps of factory patches and tones
*.syx
*.SYX
*.mid

# Roland manuals, service notes and third-party datasheets
reference/*.pdf
reference/*_OM*
reference/*service*
reference/*SERVICE*

# Photos of real hardware (copyright of whoever took them)
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.JPG

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything else, from upstream emu110
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.DS_STORE
*._
.claude/
.claude.json
*.pem

# Audacity working projects -- regenerable, and large
*.aup3
*.aup3-unsaved/

# MAME's -log output: hundreds of MB, regenerated by tools/render_u110.py --log
error.log
